thread:
maria-support: heads up — customer (ProcureCo) says their AP system rejected our invoice. procurement says vendor name doesn't match legal entity on their PO and VAT ID missing for EU invoice. they won't process the payment.
devin-finance: can you drop the PO number and the exact rejection reason? screenshot if possible. are they in the EU or outside?
maria-support: PO #PC-4421. rejection note: 'Vendor legal name mismatch — PO expects "Redwood Inference, Inc.". VAT/Tax ID required.' They attached the bank rejection screenshot and the PO PDF. Link: https://redwood-files/procureco/pc-4421.pdf :frowning:
hamid-engineering: assigning to eng to triage template. quick glance: the PDF renderer currently uses `billing.name` which is our short display name ("Redwood"), not `legal_entity.name`. That would explain the mismatch.
zoe-design: layout note — our current header stacks address lines and sometimes truncates the company suffix on wraps. procurement systems do strict string matching, so the truncation matters.
maria-support: customer also said the remit address is the old HQ address. PO expects the registered remit address (the one on their vendor master). we updated legal entity recently in system — maybe template didn't pick it up.
devin-finance: action items: (1) include full legal name exactly as registered; (2) add a distinct "Remit to" block that contains remit_address lines, country, and tax_id/vat_number when present; (3) include a machine-friendly line: `VendorTaxID: <value>` so AP can parse it. This is what ProcureCo needs.
hamid-engineering: probable root cause: invoice generator sources data from `customer_billing` table instead of the `vendor_registry` table we populate on onboarding. Fix path: change template variables to `vendor_registry.display_name`, `vendor_registry.legal_name`, `vendor_registry.remit_to.address_lines`, `vendor_registry.vat_id`. Also add optional `vat_id` row only when `country in EU_COUNTRIES` or `vat_id != null`.
hamid-engineering: quick patch suggestion — template snippet (mustache) to include legal entity and VAT:
```mustache
{{#vendor_registry.legal_name}}
  {{vendor_registry.legal_name}}
{{/vendor_registry.legal_name}}
{{#vendor_registry.vat_id}}
  VAT ID: {{vendor_registry.vat_id}}
{{/vendor_registry.vat_id}}
Remit to:
{{#vendor_registry.remit_to}}
  {{.address_line1}}
  {{.address_line2}}
  {{.city}}, {{.region}} {{.postal_code}}
  {{.country}}
{{/vendor_registry.remit_to}}
```
zoe-design: also request: use non-breaking spaces for the suffix (e.g., "Redwood Inference,\u00A0Inc.") so it doesn't wrap incorrectly. I'll update the CSS/print styles to prevent mid-word breaks for company names.
maria-support: customer also mentioned a card decline earlier in the day for a different invoice; they attempted card then Procurement blocked ACH. we should include a line in the invoice email telling customers to match vendor legal name in their vendor master to avoid declines.
devin-finance: please include a small compatibility note on the invoice PDF metadata (hidden) with `VendorLegalName` and `VendorTaxID` fields so AP systems can auto-parse. That metadata can be embedded as XMP or in the PDF Info dictionary.
hamid-engineering: I'll create a branch to change the template vars + include metadata fields. ETA for a hotfix: 1 business day for template change and 2 for production rollout after QA. Need support to repro with the attached PO and a sample vendor_registry record.
maria-support: I'll repro locally and attach sample vendor_registry record that matches the customer's expected legal name and VAT. attaching sample JSON below.
```json
{
  "vendor_registry": {
    "legal_name": "Redwood Inference, Inc.",
    "display_name": "Redwood",
    "vat_id": "GB999999973",
    "remit_to": {
      "address_line1": "55 Market St",
      "address_line2": "Suite 200",
      "city": "San Francisco",
      "region": "CA",
      "postal_code": "94105",
      "country": "United States"
    }
  }
}
```
zoe-design: thanks. once hamid ships the var change I'll mock up the layout so the legal name and VAT are visually prominent but still fit on the single-line header for small screens/print.
devin-finance: after fix, finance will run a quick batch to regenerate outstanding invoices for customers who reported procurement rejects this week.
invoices-bot: action created: TKT-1287 "Invoice PDF: use vendor_registry.legal_name + remit_to block + VAT metadata" assigned to hamid-engineering, priority: high.
maria-support: great — I'll update the ProcureCo ticket with our plan and tentative timeline. cc @devin-finance @zoe-design. :thumbsup:
hamid-engineering: noted. will post PR link here when ready.
maria-support: thanks team — keeping this thread open until ProcureCo confirms payment processed.
